Package: rcupp
Type: Package
Title: 'Rcpp' Bridge to a Fixed 'CUDA' GPU Operator Library
Version: 0.0.2
Date: 2026-11-16
Authors@R: person("Joe", "Zhu", email = "sha.joe.zhu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Joe Zhu [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Joe Zhu <sha.joe.zhu@gmail.com>
Description: Lightweight, low-level 'Rcpp'/'CUDA' bridge exposing a fixed set of GPU linear
    algebra operators and a GPU 'FISTA' solver for the Gaussian lasso. Device
    memory is kept resident across the whole solver loop, and a session API
    (persistent device X / 'cuBLAS'-handle reuse) keeps state resident across
    repeated fits such as lambda paths and cross-validation. A public C API
    (inst/include/rcupp.h, R_RegisterCCallable/R_GetCCallable) lets downstream
    packages LinkingTo: 'rcupp' and call the operators and session from their
    own C++ code, making 'rcupp' a reusable 'CUDA'-for-'Rcpp' framework. The 'CUDA'
    Toolkit is optional: without it a supported CPU fallback implements the
    same 'FISTA' solver AND the same public C API (including sessions), so the
    package stays installable, runnable and checkable everywhere (no GPU
    acceleration).
